"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Favorable findings include negative surgical margins, absence of seminal vesicle invasion, absence of lymphovascular invasion, and no lymph node metastasis. The preoperative PSA was elevated at 11. The surgical pathology indicated a Gleason 4+5 (ISUP grade group 5) and pathological stage pT2c, with no extraprostatic extension. Countervailing factors include the missing biopsy grade and ISUP report, which widens uncertainty regarding the true tumor biology. The nodal status was documented as negative. The primary uncertainty lies in the missing postoperative PSA and subsequent trajectory, which is critical for monitoring recurrence. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and their trend would significantly revise this prognosis. The current heuristic horizon suggests a range for recurrence monitoring. The fixed estimated horizon is 50.20 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 37.65–62.75 months; its coverage has not been validated."
